    "concept": "records",
    "title": "Records",
    "explanation": "The warehouse's inventory computer, the robot's friend, keeps a record for every crate: facts about one crate kept together, each with a name, like its number and whether it holds the key. The robot asks for one fact by its name: crate.number.",
    "realWords": [
      { "word": "interface", "code": "interface", "text": "An interface describes a shape: the name of each part and its type. Every Crate has the same parts, so code that is handed a Crate knows what is inside before it looks." },
      { "word": "property", "text": "Each named part of an object is a property. A dot reads one: crate.number is the number property of crate. Records, places and robots are all objects with properties." }
    ],
    "demo": {
      "world": {
